   "date": "2020-04-26T15:59:57Z",
   "subject": "Resolução espacial",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Olá Filipe,<div><br></div><div>quando aplico a função aggregate (pacote Raster) para identificar a resolução da imagem, qual é a unidade do valor de saída? A função me retornou 0.00642, isso seria 0.6 cm? Grato.</div><div><br></div><div>Igor Cobelo</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "m178aAV8AgAJ",
   "from": "fmatias",
   "author": "c59b667c61f258ae",
   "date": "2020-04-27T16:42:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: Resolução espacial",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Olá Igor,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">A unidade do pixel será a mesma da foto original. Então, se sua resolução\r\noriginal está em metros, após a função aggregate() a saída se manterá em\r\nmetros. Na verdade, o que muda e o tamanho do pixel, mas a unidade se mantem a\r\nmesma. Geralmente fotos de drones nos dá a informação em metros e algumas imagens\r\nde satélites nos informa em Km.  Assim, se vc tem uma imagem com resolução\r\noriginal de 0.05m=5cm ao usar a função aggregate() com fact=2, a resolução da\r\nimagem nova será  algo como 0.1m=10cm, e\r\npor ai vai. Por favor veja que existem várias perguntas online relacionadas,\r\ncomo nos links abaixo:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:black\"><a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/32278825/how-to-change-the-resolution-of-a-raster-layer-in-r\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/32278825/how-to-change-the-resolution-of-a-raster-layer-in-r&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242225275000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nk0juDYp5P_fXBLFT86is\">https://stackoverflow.com/questions/32278825/how-to-change-the-resolution-of-a-raster-layer-in-r</a></span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"color:black\"><a href=\"https://gis.stackexchange.com/questions/255150/using-resample-vs-aggregate-extend-in-r-to-have-rasters-of-matching-resolutio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gis.stackexchange.com/questions/255150/using-resample-vs-aggregate-extend-in-r-to-have-rasters-of-matching-resolutio&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242225275000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3-eOBlJL0N7ogpURtR56Kc\">https://gis.stackexchange.com/questions/255150/using-resample-vs-aggregate-extend-in-r-to-have-rasters-of-matching-resolutio</a></span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Espero que tenha respondido sua pergunta.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Abs<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Filipe <u></u><u></u></span></p>"
    ]
   ]
